Our understanding of dust properties has primarily been shaped by infrared observations in the Milky Way (Molinari et al. 2010; Planck Collaboration et al. 2014; Csengeri et al. 2016; Planck Collaboration et al. 2016, e.g.,), which reveal that dust properties may vary in different ISM environments. However, the connection between these variations to large-scale galactic structures, such as spiral arms and rings, remains poorly understood. The edge-on projection of the Milky Way and the ambiguity of line-of-sight distances pose significant challenges to achieving a comprehensive, panoramic view of dust properties.

